## FINAL GAME DESIGN PRINCIPLE

CREASE CLASH must become a cricket contest.

The batter must make decisions, read deliveries, select shots, time contact, find gaps and decide when to run.

The bowler must create pressure through pace, line, length, movement, delivery variation and field placement.

Fielders must make a difference.

Mistimed shots must have consequences.

Well-executed shots must be rewarded.

Running between wickets must matter.

Both multiplayer players must have their own correct gameplay interface.

**The goal is not to make the ball fly further or add more buttons. The goal is to make every delivery a meaningful contest in which batting, bowling, fielding and running all contribute to the result.**